lessons.lesson:
`if` runs a block when its condition is true; `else` covers the other case, and
`else if` chains more tests.

```ts
if (score >= 90) {
  console.log("A");
} else if (score >= 80) {
  console.log("B");
} else {
  console.log("C");
}
```

Only the first matching branch runs.

